h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 727)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Camera raw develops with ARRI&#8217;s own tool.</b> Drop ARRIRAW and press <b>Develop</b>: Asobi now uses ARRI Reference Tool (ART CMD) first &#8212; ARRI&#8217;s reference color, and several times faster than real time (three clips, 10 GB, under a minute). It is a free download Asobi isn&#8217;t allowed to carry, so the first time it offers <b>Get ARRI&#8217;s Free Tool&#8230;</b> and <b>Locate art-cmd&#8230;</b>; point at the unzipped folder once. DaVinci Resolve Studio remains the fallback when the tool isn&#8217;t there.</li>
<li>If a clip can&#8217;t be developed, the message now says why in the tool&#8217;s own words &#8212; or that macOS isn&#8217;t letting Asobi read the drive.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
