h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 724)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>ARRIRAW opens.</b> Drop camera-original <code>.mxf</code> files and Asobi names them (&#8220;ARRIRAW (HDE) &#183; ALEXA Mini LF&#8221;) and, on a Mac with DaVinci Resolve Studio, offers <b>Develop in Resolve</b>: Resolve runs without a window, develops each clip to Log C at half size and quits; the clips join the playlist as they land, under their own names and timecode, shown through LogC3 (LogC4 for an ALEXA 35). Developed once, they simply open next time. Quit Resolve first &#8212; Asobi won&#8217;t take over a Resolve you have open.</li>
<li><b>Compare keeps each clip&#8217;s own shape.</b> Comparing two spots with different aspect ratios stretched the second to match the first. B now keeps its own aspect in every compare mode &#8212; side by side, stacked, wipe, mix and difference &#8212; and in frame grabs and reports.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
